gbbe(){return"Dorian"},
gbgB(){return"Three colours of scale"},
gbgz(){return"A major scale sounds bright and happy. Listen to it climb."},
gbgA(){return"A minor scale sounds darker \u2014 its 3rd, 6th and 7th steps sit a little lower."},
gbgy(){return"Dorian is like minor, but its 6th step is raised \u2014 so it sounds minor with a brighter twist. That one note is the whole secret!"},
